exists_continuous_zero_one_of_isClosed.code:
exists_continuous_zero_one_of_isClosed.{u_1} {X : Type u_1} [TopologicalSpace X] [NormalSpace X] {s t : Set X}
  (hs : IsClosed s) (ht : IsClosed t) (hd : Disjoint s t) :
  ∃ f, EqOn (⇑f) 0 s ∧ EqOn (⇑f) 1 t ∧ ∀ (x : X), f x ∈ Icc 0 1

exists_continuous_zero_one_of_isClosed.comment:
Urysohn's lemma: if `s` and `t` are two disjoint closed sets in a normal topological space `X`,
then there exists a continuous function `f : X → ℝ` such that

* `f` equals zero on `s`;
* `f` equals one on `t`;
* `0 ≤ f x ≤ 1` for all `x`.

